    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0149" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72116/532</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">21 February, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I must say I am afraid
                    of <hi rendition="#underline">any</hi> expression of policy framed jointly at
                    Paris. There has been none yet that seemed to me even touched with wisdom. I see
                    that you have sought to suggest and safeguard, but I am afraid that statesmen
                    like our friend L—G. will not care to be guided and will rather rejoice in a
                    somewhat crude and cynical rejoinder to the Red Cross.</p>
                <p>I approve the despatch to Sharp, however, and am quite willing to subscribe to a
                    proper reply if they will let us see it beforehand. Sharp can cable it, and the
                    delay will not be serious.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
